---
import Document from "../layouts/Document.astro";
import { site } from "../data/universe";
---

<Document
  title="There is room at the table."
  label="The community commons"
  description="Discuss the lore, share a Coneposting experiment, propose a story or help maintain the official All Hail the Cone archive."
>
  <h2>A place to begin</h2>
  <p>
    The community begins in the official GitHub repository. Bring an
    observation, a drawing, a story, or a useful correction. You do not need to
    know everything in the archive to take part.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a class="button button-primary" href={`${site.repo}/discussions`}>
      Enter the discussions ↗
    </a>
  </p>
  <h2>Three ways to contribute</h2>
  <h3>Explore the world</h3>
  <p>
    Discuss a character, ask about a crossing, or offer an interpretation. Label
    theories as theories. A popular explanation does not become canon by
    repetition.
  </p>
  <h3>Make something</h3>
  <p>
    Share a story, image or experiment using the{" "}
    <a href={`${site.repo}/issues/new?template=creative-proposal.yml`}>
      creative proposal form
    </a>
    . Include your sources, how it was made, and the permission you hold to
    submit it. Fan work begins as Coneposting unless an editorial decision says
    otherwise.
  </p>
  <h3>Improve the archive</h3>
  <p>
    Report broken pages, accessibility barriers and inconsistent records using
    the{" "}
    <a href={`${site.repo}/issues/new?template=bug-report.yml`}>issue form</a>.
    Code and content improvements can be proposed through a pull request.
  </p>
  <h2>Hospitality is a practice</h2>
  <p>
    Be kind to people, precise about disagreements and respectful of boundaries.
    No harassment, hate, impersonation, spam, exposed private information or
    stolen work. Critique a contribution without demeaning its creator.
  </p>
  <p>
    Maintainers may label, move, close or remove contributions that violate
    these rules. Report a concern using GitHub’s reporting tools; do not repost
    private information in a public issue.
  </p>
  <h2>How an idea becomes official</h2>
  <p>
    A maintainer reviews tone, visual consistency, provenance and the effect on
    existing stories. Acceptance is explicit and recorded. Submission is not
    automatic acceptance, a transfer of ownership, or a promise of compensation.
  </p>
  <p>
    Read the{" "}
    <a href={`${site.repo}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}>contribution guide</a>{" "}
    and <a href={`${site.repo}/blob/main/ART_GUIDE.md`}>art guide</a> before
    preparing a larger contribution.
  </p>
</Document>
